    "passage": "Sometimes, unintentional acts may lead to remarkable outcomes. Wordle, a renowned online word puzzle game, is one such example. Its journey from a simple creation to a global phenomenon is [[1]] surprising and inspiring.\nCreated by software engineer Josh Wardle as a small project for his game-loving wife during the COVID-19 pandemic, Wordle started quietly with just 90 players. Without any marketing or elaborate planning, it spread purely through word of mouth, attracting millions. This heartfelt idea eventually grew into a global sensation that no one, including its creator, [[2]].\nWordle is extremely popular because it offers a quick yet engaging [[3]]. It challenges players to guess the correct word composed of five letters in fewer than six tries every day. Easy as the game is, it makes you feel clever, [[4]] through language skills or logical deduction.\nEventually, Wardle sold Wordle to The New York Times for a seven-figure sum. His story teaches us that even [[5]] ordinary ideas have the potential to grow into something big. Just like Wordle, an idea born out of love and creativity can unexpectedly become a worldwide success.",
